<title>GERMANY: MAN says 1995/96 group net profit rises.</title>
<headline>MAN says 1995/96 group net profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			   330     vs 272</p>
<p>    Group income from ord. activities    500     vs 358</p>
<p>    Group earnings per share		 26.00   vs 22.70 marks</p>
<p>    Group sales				  20,270  vs 18,602</p>
<p>    Dividend				     12	vs 9.50 marks</p>
<p>    Group incoming orders		    20,787  vs 20,602</p>
<p>    Group orders in hand		     17,621  vs 16,891</p>
<p>Group incoming orders by division</p>
<p>     -- Commercial vehicles		  7,539   vs 7,734</p>
<p>     -- Printing machines		    2,235   vs 2,379</p>
<p>     -- Diesel motors			  1,703   vs 1,658</p>
<p>     -- Other machinery/plant sales	5,761   vs 5,342</p>
<p>     -- Trading				  3,954   vs 3,860</p>
<p>     -- Consolidation loss		     405   vs 371 loss</p>
<p>Group incoming orders by region</p>
<p>     -- Domestic				 6,567   vs 7,059</p>
<p>     -- Foreign				  14,220  vs 13,543</p>
<p>Group sales by division</p>
<p>     -- Commercial vehicles		  7,984   vs 7,236</p>
<p>     -- Printing machines		    2,361   vs 2,002</p>
<p>     -- Diesel motors			  1,529   vs 1,607</p>
<p>     -- Other machinery/plant sales	4,896   vs 4,103</p>
<p>     -- Trading				  3,837   vs 4,028</p>
<p>     -- Consolidation loss		     337   vs 374 loss</p>
<p>Group sales by region</p>
<p>     -- Domestic				 7,039   vs 7,056</p>
<p>     -- Foreign				  13,231  vs 11,546</p>
<p>    Group workforce			    57,813  vs 56,503</p>
<p>     -- Domestic				 45,923  vs 45,085</p>
<p>     -- Foreign				  11,890  vs 11,418</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German industrial group is MAN AG.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
